---
/**
 * PRIVACY & COOKIES
 * The statistics and newsletter paragraphs appear automatically once
 * SITE.umamiWebsiteId / SITE.brevoFormAction are filled in (site.config.ts),
 * so this page always describes what the website actually does.
 * Change SITE.privacyUpdated whenever you change this page.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
const updated = new Date(SITE.privacyUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
const email = SITE.contactEmail;
const stats = !!SITE.umamiWebsiteId;
const news = !!SITE.brevoFormAction;
const ext = (href: string, label: string) => `<a href="${href}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">${label}<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy & Cookies" description="How the Tarkasa Tales website handles personal data: no cookies, cookieless visitor statistics, an optional email newsletter, and nothing collected from children.">
  <div class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
    <article class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-4">
      <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl">Privacy &amp; Cookies</h1>
      <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-card)] bg-mint-soft p-6 text-plum-deep">
        <h2 class="text-2xl !text-plum-deep">The short version</h2>
        <ul class="prose-tt mt-3">
          <li>This website does not set any cookies and does not use advertising or social media trackers.</li>
          {stats
            ? <li>We count visits with Umami, a privacy-friendly statistics tool that uses no cookies and cannot identify you.</li>
            : <li>This website does not run visitor statistics.</li>}
          {news
            ? <li>Our email newsletter is optional. You only receive it if you sign up and confirm, and you can unsubscribe at any time.</li>
            : <li>We do not run a newsletter.</li>}
          <li>We do not ask for or collect information from children.</li>
          <li>Free downloads never require you to sign up.</li>
          <li>Books are bought on Amazon, where Amazon’s own privacy notice applies.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-tt">
        <h2>Who is responsible for this website</h2>
        <p>This website is run by Tarkasa Tales{SITE.privacyController ? <>: {SITE.privacyController}</> : ''}, the data controller under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).{email && <> You can contact us about privacy at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</>}</p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>The website is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare necessarily processes technical information — such as your IP address, browser type and the page requested — to deliver pages to you and to protect the website against abuse and attacks. Cloudflare processes this information on our behalf. You can read more in <Fragment set:html={ext('https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/', 'Cloudflare’s privacy policy')} />.</p>
        <p>Fonts and images are served from this website itself, so your browser does not contact font or image services run by other companies when you read our pages.</p>

        <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
        {stats ? (
          <>
            <p>To understand which pages are useful and how visitors find us, we use <strong>Umami Cloud</strong>, hosted in the European Union. Umami does not use cookies, local storage or any other identifier stored on your device, and it does not build a profile of you. It records the page you visit, the website or campaign link you came from, your country, your browser and device type, and simple actions such as clicking a “Buy on Amazon” store button, downloading a free activity or submitting the newsletter form. Your IP address is not stored. Because no one can be identified, we do not need to ask for consent and we do not show a cookie banner.</p>
            <p>If your browser sends a “Do Not Track” signal, no statistics are recorded at all. Our legal basis is our legitimate interest in improving the website. Umami acts as our processor; see <Fragment set:html={ext('https://umami.is/privacy', 'Umami’s privacy policy')} />.</p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <p>This website does not currently run visitor statistics or analytics tools.</p>
        )}

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>This website does not set cookies and does not use similar technologies such as tracking pixels or local storage for tracking. That is why there is no cookie banner. If that ever changes, we will update this page first and ask for your consent where the law requires it.</p>

        <h2>Email newsletter</h2>
        {news ? (
          <>
            <p>You can choose to receive our newsletter for parents and teachers: about one email a month with a free printable, a scientist story and news about new books. We ask for your email address and, if you like, your first name. You must be 16 or older to sign up. After you sign up, we send one email asking you to confirm; you are only added to the list once you click the confirmation link.</p>
            <p>We send the newsletter with <strong>Brevo</strong> (Sendinblue SAS, France), which stores your details in the European Union on our behalf under a data processing agreement. Brevo records the date of your signup and confirmation and whether you open or click our emails, so we can see what is useful. See <Fragment set:html={ext('https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/', 'Brevo’s privacy policy')} />.</p>
            <p>Our legal basis is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time with the unsubscribe link at the bottom of every email, or by emailing us. When you unsubscribe we stop sending emails straight away, and we delete your details within 30 days, except a record that you unsubscribed so you are never emailed again by mistake. We never sell or share your details, and the free downloads on this website never require you to sign up.</p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <p>We do not run a newsletter at the moment. If we start one, it will be optional and this page will explain how it works before it goes live.</p>
        )}

        <h2>When you email us</h2>
        <p>If you choose to email us, we receive your email address, your name if you include it, and whatever you write. We use this only to read and reply to your message, and we keep it only as long as needed for that conversation. We do not add you to mailing lists unless you ask us to. Our legal basis is our legitimate interest in replying to messages people send us.</p>

        <h2>Links to Amazon and other websites</h2>
        <p>Our “Buy on Amazon” buttons take you to Amazon’s website, where purchases, payment, delivery and customer service are handled entirely by Amazon, and Amazon’s privacy notice applies. Some links we share on social media and in our emails include an Amazon Attribution tag, which lets Amazon tell us, in total numbers only, how many books were bought after people followed links from a particular place (for example, Instagram). We never receive your name, address or payment details from Amazon. We do not currently use Amazon affiliate links; if we start to, we will say so on this page and next to the links.</p>
        <p>We also link to our social media pages. These are only links: this website does not embed social media posts or load anything from those services. If you visit them, their own privacy policies apply.</p>

        <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
        <p>Our books are for children, but this website is designed for parents, grandparents, teachers and librarians. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children, and our newsletter is only for people aged 16 or older. If you are a child, please ask a parent, carer or teacher to contact us for you.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to ask for access to, correction of, or deletion of personal data we hold about you, to withdraw your consent, and to object to how we use it. To make a request, please contact us{email ? <> at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></> : ' using the details on our contact page'}. You also have the right to complain to a data protection authority. In the Netherlands this is the <Fragment set:html={ext('https://www.autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl/', 'Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens')} />.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change how this website works, for example by adding a contact form or a new tool, we will update this page first and change the date at the top.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
